+# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+# [MP8] T52 wall-stuck self-rescue (2026-09-02)
+# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+#
+# A player's exact words on 2026-09-01 - "The duck walked up to the stone wall and suddenly WASD stopped responding,
+# **but right-click crouch still worked**, so it definitely wasn't clicking into another window, and the spot happened to be where the hunter couldn't snipe me, so the game got stuck."
+#
+# 🩸 The line "right-click crouch still worked" rules out the entire input layer in one go — because `update_crouch()` is
+# the **last line** of `_process`, placed **after** the three gates `PauseMenu.active` / `game_focused` / `active`
+# and the `movement_input` assignment. Crouch works ⇒ all three gates passed and `movement_input` has a value.
+# The problem can only be on the `move_and_slide()` side. **The player is stuck in geometry.**
+#
+# ⚠️ This overturns the premise of the roll-call logger in this mod's 1.5 — all it prints is "character present, activated,
+#    window focused=true", and that **is exactly what this bug looks like**. The check itself asked the wrong question and has been fixed too.
+#
+# Ruled-out hypothesis (don't go down this road again) - **it is not crouching through walls**. probe81 measured it. The duck has two body colliders,
+# `StandingCollision` (height 5.00, radius 0.70) and `CrouchCollision` (height 3.60, **same radius 0.70**),
+# and crouching only disables the former. **It only gets shorter, not narrower**, so it can neither pass into a wall nor squeeze into a gap.
+#
+# This approach doesn't hunt for that specific wall — there may be more than one spot on the map, and the consequence is **the whole match stuck**
+# (the player also said "the spot happened to be where the hunter couldn't snipe me", so they couldn't even escape by getting shot). So we add a general safety net.
+#
+#   **Input held, but barely moved for N seconds straight → teleport back to the breadcrumb position from 1 m back.**
+#
+# The breadcrumb "updates once you are more than 1 m from the previous breadcrumb", so it is always about one meter back along your path —
+# teleporting there = stepping back along the way you came, which always frees you, and the move is small enough to be nearly invisible.
+#
+# ⚠️ Runs **only on the player's own machine**. The duck's movement authority is the player themselves (`set_multiplayer_authority`),
+#    everyone else's copy has `_physics_process` turned off, and the server can't detect this either.
+# ⚠️ Standing against a wall for 3 seconds also triggers it, at the cost of being pushed back one meter — barely noticeable,
+#    whereas missing one real stuck case ruins a whole match. This asymmetry was chosen on purpose.
+const MP8_STUCK_SECONDS: float = 3.0    # How long it must last to count as stuck
+const MP8_STUCK_EPSILON: float = 0.05   # Per-frame movement below this counts as "not moving"
+const MP8_CRUMB_DISTANCE: float = 1.0   # Breadcrumb spacing
+
+var _mp8_stuck_t: float = 0.0
+var _mp8_prev_pos: Vector3 = Vector3.ZERO
+var _mp8_crumb: Vector3 = Vector3.ZERO
+var _mp8_crumb_set: bool = false
+
 
 var run_blend: float = 0.0
 
@@ -183,9 +223,54 @@ func _physics_process(delta: float) -> void :
 	move_and_slide()
 	update_bump()
 
+	_mp8_check_stuck(delta)
+
 	update_animations(delta)
 	play_footstep_sound(delta)
 
+# [MP8] T52 - input held but not moving → step back one meter along the path. See the section at the top of the file.
+func _mp8_check_stuck(delta: float) -> void :
+
+	if not _mp8_crumb_set:
+		_mp8_crumb = global_position
+		_mp8_prev_pos = global_position
+		_mp8_crumb_set = true
+		return
+
+	var moved: float = global_position.distance_to(_mp8_prev_pos)
+	_mp8_prev_pos = global_position
+
+	# Once you've walked far enough, drop a new breadcrumb (it is always about one meter back along your path)
+	if global_position.distance_to(_mp8_crumb) > MP8_CRUMB_DISTANCE:
+		_mp8_crumb = global_position
+
+	# No direction key held means not stuck — standing still is the player's own choice
+	if movement_input.length() <= Globals.Epsilon:
+		_mp8_stuck_t = 0.0
+		return
+
+	if moved > MP8_STUCK_EPSILON:
+		_mp8_stuck_t = 0.0
+		return
+
+	_mp8_stuck_t += delta
+	if _mp8_stuck_t < MP8_STUCK_SECONDS:
+		return
+
+	# Reaching here means a direction key is held and there has been no movement for MP8_STUCK_SECONDS seconds straight
+	# ⚠️ Always print the coordinates — it's our only way to find out "where that wall is".
+	#    It can't be reproduced locally, so we have to rely on player logs.
+	print("[MP8] 🩸 Duck Hunt stuck self-rescue: %s at (%.1f, %.1f, %.1f) held a direction key for %.1f s without moving, moved back to (%.1f, %.1f, %.1f) (T52)" % [
+		player_presence.network_name if player_presence else "?",
+		global_position.x, global_position.y, global_position.z,
+		_mp8_stuck_t,
+		_mp8_crumb.x, _mp8_crumb.y, _mp8_crumb.z,
+	])
+
+	_mp8_stuck_t = 0.0
+	teleport_rpc.rpc(_mp8_crumb)
+
+
